\section{Experiments}
\subsection{Setup}
\paragraph{Evaluation.} We report Top-1 accuracy on the IID test set; on SCUBA (higher is better, reduced background bias) averaged over background types; on SCUFO (lower is better, reduced foreground/static bias); on Confl-FG, where a conflicting foreground is inserted on a sinusoid SCUBA background to isolate foreground effects (higher is better); and the \emph{contrasted accuracy}, where a prediction counts as correct iff the model is correct on a SCUBA clip and incorrect on its SCUFO counterpart, capturing simultaneous background and foreground debiasing. We use HMDB51 \citep{kuehne2011hmdb} and UCF101 \citep{soomro2012ucf101} (with our improved protocol), and the ARAS rare-scene OOD benchmark.

\paragraph{Implementation.} The backbone is Video Swin-T \citep{liu2022video} pretrained on Kinetics-400 \citep{carreira2017quo}, with 32 frames per clip at stride 2 and $224\times224$ resolution. Augmentations are random resized crop and horizontal flip. We use AdamW \citep{loshchilov2017decoupled} ($\beta_1=0.9$, $\beta_2=0.999$), weight decay 0.01, base learning rate $10^{-4}$ at batch size 64, 5 warmup epochs and a cosine schedule. We compare with Mixup \citep{zhang2017mixup}, VideoMix \citep{yun2020videomix}, SDN \citep{choi2019can}, BE \citep{wang2021removing}, ActorCutMix \citep{zou2023learning}, FAME \citep{ding2022motion} and StillMix \citep{li2023mitigating}.

